---
# Static analysis for the libFuzzer targets, extending the root config rather than replacing it.
# The filter adds fuzz/include, so the decoder the three targets share is analyzed as well.
# Two checks are dropped, neither saying anything true about a differential harness:
# - readability-magic-numbers: the widths the owners are instantiated at, the case labels of the
#   operation switch, and the slack past a width that out-of-range inputs reach for. Naming each
#   would say the same thing twice and hide the list.
# - readability-function-cognitive-complexity: each target is one switch over its operations,
#   every case a few lines applying one operation to the owner and its model. Splitting it into a
#   function per case moves the switch rather than simplifying it.
InheritParentConfig: true
HeaderFilterRegex: '(include/xstd|fuzz/include)/.*'
Checks: >
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity
